---@class customerio.AddCollectionRequestBodyCase1
---@field name string The name of the collection. This is how you'll reference your collection in messages—`{{collection_name.data-property}}`.
---@field url string The URL for your CSV or JSON data. Customer.io detects the format from the `Content-Type` that your URL returns, or from the file extension if the `Content-Type` doesn't say. JSON data can be an array of objects or one object per line. CSV data needs a header row, and Customer.io reads every CSV value as a string.
---@field delete_field? string An attribute that marks a row for deletion, like `deleted`. When a row in a write request or a synced file sets this attribute to `true`, or to the text `true`, `1`, or `yes` in any case, Customer.io deletes the row with the same key instead of saving it. Deleting a key that doesn't exist does nothing. Customer.io never keeps a row that this attribute marks. When you create or replace a collection, Customer.io leaves marked rows out. When you set a delete field on an existing collection, Customer.io deletes the rows it already marks. A row that isn't marked keeps the attribute as you sent it. The delete field can't be the same as the key field. Send an empty string to remove it.
---@field key_field? string The attribute that holds each row's unique key, like `sku`, similar to a primary key in a database table. Set a key field to add, change, delete, or read individual rows without replacing the whole collection. Each row needs a unique, non-empty string or number in this attribute, up to 1,024 bytes.

