---@class customerio.BroadcastStatusRequest
---@field broadcast_id number The ID of the broadcast that you want to return information about.
---@field trigger_id number The ID of the automation trigger that you want to return information for.

---@class customerio.BroadcastStatusResponse
---@field trigger? customerio.BroadcastStatusResponseTrigger You can get triggers to know when you triggered a broadcast and whether or not it's been processed.

---You can get triggers to know when you triggered a broadcast and whether or not it's been processed.
---@class customerio.BroadcastStatusResponseTrigger
---@field audience_count? number The number of people in the trigger's audience. For a send without a `rate_limit`, we set it when the send finishes. For a rate-limited send, we set it when the first people enter. It is `0` until then.
---@field broadcast_id? number The identifier for a broadcast.
---@field cancelled_at? number The date-time you canceled this trigger, or `0` if you haven't canceled it.
---@field created_at? number The date time when the referenced ID was created.
---@field expires_after? number The send window in seconds that you set when you triggered the broadcast, or `0` if the send has no expiry.
---@field id? number The identifier for a broadcast trigger.
---@field processed_at? number The date-time when Customer.io processed the trigger.
---@field rate_limit? customerio.BroadcastStatusResponseTriggerRateLimit The rate limit you set when you triggered the broadcast. We omit this field if you didn't set one.
---@field scheduled_at? number The date-time this trigger is scheduled to send at, or `0` if you didn't schedule it.

---The rate limit you set when you triggered the broadcast. We omit this field if you didn't set one.
---@class customerio.BroadcastStatusResponseTriggerRateLimit
---@field period? customerio.BroadcastStatusResponseTriggerRateLimitPeriod The length of each period.
---@field rate? number The maximum number of people that enter the broadcast in each `period`.
---@field spread? boolean Whether we let people in at an even pace across the period.

---The length of each period.
---@alias customerio.BroadcastStatusResponseTriggerRateLimitPeriod "minute"|"hour"|"day"

---@class customerio.CampaignActionLinksRequest
---@field campaign_id number The ID of the automation that you want to trigger or return information about.
---@field action_id number The action you want to lookup or act on.
---@field period? customerio.CampaignActionLinksRequestPeriod|string The unit of time for your report.
---@field steps? number The number of periods you want to return. Defaults to the maximum available, or `12` if the period is in `months`. Maximums are 24 hours, 45 days, 12 weeks, or 121 months. Days start at 00:00 EST. Weeks start at 00:00 EST on Sunday. Months start at 00:00 EST on the 1st of the month.
---@field type? customerio.CampaignActionLinksRequestType|string The type of item you want to return metrics for. When empty, the response contains metrics for all possible types.
---@field unique? boolean If true, the response contains only unique customer results, i.e. a customer who clicks a link twice is only counted once. If false, the response contains the total number of results without regard to uniqueness.

---@alias customerio.CampaignActionLinksRequestPeriod "hours"|"days"|"weeks"|"months"

---@alias customerio.CampaignActionLinksRequestType "email"|"webhook"|"twilio"|"whatsapp"|"slack"|"push"|"in_app"|"live_notification"

