---@class customerio.CampaignActionMetricsRequest
---@field campaign_id number The ID of the automation that you want to trigger or return information about.
---@field action_id number The action in the automation. If the action is a message with translations, you can pass the `id` of the action to get metrics for a specific language variant or pass the `multi_language_branch_action_id` to get metrics for each language variant and total metrics across the variants.
---@field version? customerio.CampaignActionMetricsRequestVersion|string Send `2`. We recommend version 2: it takes an explicit window (`start`, `end`, and `res`) in the time zone you pass as `tz`. Any other value, including leaving the parameter off, uses version 1: a window derived from `period` and `steps`, always in Eastern time.
---@field res? customerio.CampaignActionMetricsRequestRes|string **Version 2.** Required when you send `version=2`. Sets the increment for each point in the series—hourly, daily, weekly, or monthly.
---@field start? number **Version 2.** Required when you send `version=2`. The unix timestamp for the beginning of your metrics.
---@field ["end"]? number **Version 2.** Required when you send `version=2`. The unix timestamp for the end of your metrics. Limited to 10 years from the `start` parameter.
---@field tz? string **Version 2.** The time zone for the window you request. Defaults to UTC. Use the [region format](/messaging/send/timezones/example-timezones/#region-format).
---@field period? customerio.CampaignActionMetricsRequestPeriod|string **Version 1.** The unit of time for your report. Send `version=2` and set `res` instead.
---@field steps? number **Version 1.** The number of periods you want to return. Defaults to the maximum available, or `12` if the period is in `months`. Maximums are 24 hours, 45 days, 12 weeks, or 121 months. Days start at 00:00 EST, weeks at 00:00 EST on Sunday, months at 00:00 EST on the 1st. Send `version=2` and set `start` and `end` instead.
---@field type? customerio.CampaignActionMetricsRequestType|string The type of item you want to return metrics for. When empty, the response contains metrics for all possible types.

---@alias customerio.CampaignActionMetricsRequestPeriod "hours"|"days"|"weeks"|"months"

---@alias customerio.CampaignActionMetricsRequestRes "hours"|"hourly"|"days"|"daily"|"weeks"|"weekly"|"months"|"monthly"

---@alias customerio.CampaignActionMetricsRequestType "email"|"webhook"|"twilio"|"whatsapp"|"slack"|"push"|"in_app"|"live_notification"

---@alias customerio.CampaignActionMetricsRequestVersion "1"|"2"

---@class customerio.CampaignActionMetricsResponse
---@field ["end"]? string The end of the window we reported on, in ISO 8601 format.
---@field language_variants? customerio.CampaignActionMetricsResponseLanguageVariantsMap Metrics for each language variant of a multi-language message, keyed by the variant's action ID. Only returned when you request metrics for a multi-language branch action.
---@field metric? customerio.CampaignActionMetricsResponseMetric
---@field res? customerio.CampaignActionMetricsResponseRes The resolution we reported at.
---@field start? string The start of the window we reported on, in ISO 8601 format.

---Metrics for each language variant of a multi-language message, keyed by the variant's action ID. Only returned when you request metrics for a multi-language branch action.
