---@class customerio.CreateManSegmentResponseSegment
---@field conditions? customerio.CreateManSegmentResponseSegmentConditionsMap The conditions that determine who belongs to the segment, as a tree of nested `and` and `or` groups. Customer.io includes this object for data-driven and snapshot segments and omits it for manual segments, which don't have conditions. A profile attribute condition appears as an `attribute_change` event with a `to` filter and an inverted `from` filter, and filter values are always strings, even for numeric or boolean attributes.
---@field created_at? number The date time when the referenced ID was created.
---@field deduplicate_id? string An identifier in the format `id:timestamp` where the id is for the object you're working with (Automations, Deliveries, Exports, Identities, One-time sends, Segments, and Templates), and the timestamp is the last time the object was updated.
---@field description? string A description for the segment. This can help you understand the purpose of the segment when you encounter it in other requests or in the UI.
---@field id? number The identifier for a segment; used to target a segment in requests.
---@field name? string The name of the segment.
---@field progress? number|distilled.Null Customer.io returns `0` while the segment is in the `build` state and `null` when it's `finished`. This field doesn't report partial progress, so use `state` to tell whether the segment is still building.
---@field state? customerio.CreateManSegmentResponseSegmentState The segment's build state. The state is `build` while Customer.io calculates who belongs to the segment, and `finished` when membership is up to date.
---@field tags? customerio.CreateManSegmentResponseSegmentTagsList|distilled.Null The tags assigned to the segment, if any. Tags may help you sort through your segments.
---@field type? customerio.CreateManSegmentResponseSegmentType The type of segment. [Learn more in our segmentation docs.](/messaging/segmentation/segments/#types-of-segments)
---@field updated_at? number The date time when the referenced ID was last updated.

