---@alias customerio.CreateNewsletterLanguageVariantResponseNewsletterType "email"|"webhook"|"twilio"|"push"|"in_app"|"inbox"

---@class customerio.CreateNewsletterRequest
---@field body customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBody

---@alias customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBody customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase0|customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase1|customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase2|customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase3|customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase4|customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase5

---When you create an email, include `subject` and `body`. Set either `from` or `from_id`, but not both. If you set neither, Customer.io uses your oldest verified sending address.
---@class customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase0
---@field type customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase0Type|string The channel type for the one-time send.
---@field body string The HTML body content of the email. Use standard HTML/CSS, not syntax unique to Design Studio.
---@field name string The name of the one-time send.
---@field subject string The subject line of the email.
---@field body_plain? string The plaintext body of the email. If provided, this overwrites the auto-generated plaintext.
---@field deduped? boolean When `true`, Customer.io sends only one message per email address or phone number, even when several profiles share it. Supported on `email`, `twilio`, and `sms` one-time sends. If the send's address is an identifier in your workspace (email for `email` sends, phone number for `twilio` and `sms` sends), Customer.io returns a 422 when you set `deduped` to `true`, because no two profiles can share an identifier and there's nothing to dedupe. Leave it out to use the default for your workspace's identifier configuration. No endpoint changes this later, so set it here if you don't want the default.
---@field expires_after? number A send window in seconds, or `0` for no expiry. Customer.io stops delivering the one-time send once the window closes, so a delayed message doesn't arrive when it's no longer useful. Set it here only alongside `send_now` or `scheduled_at`, because the window runs from the send. On a plain draft, set it on the [send](/integrations/api/app/tag/send-messages/sendNewsletter/) or [schedule](/integrations/api/app/tag/send-messages/scheduleNewsletter/) call instead.
---@field from? string The address to send the email from, in the format `Name <email@domain.com>`. You can set `from` or `from_id`, but not both. Use one of the `address` values from [List sender identities](/integrations/api/app/tag/sender-identities/listSenders/).
---@field from_id? number The identifier of the `from` address, commonly known as the "sender". Use [List sender identities](/integrations/api/app/tag/sender-identities/listSenders/) to find valid IDs.
---@field layout_id? number The ID of the [layout](/journeys/channels/email/layouts/3-layouts-and-customerio/) you want to use for the email. If you don't set one, the email uses your workspace's default layout. Find a layout's ID in its URL.
---@field preheader_text? string [Also known as "preview text"](/journeys/channels/email/headers/custom-preheader-text/), this is the small block of text shown in an email inbox next to or underneath the subject line.
---@field rate_limit_email_rate? number Maximum number of messages per time period. **NOTE:** Though this states `email_rate`, you can use this for other message channels. Only fixed rate limits are supported, not [daily ramp limits](/messaging/send/broadcasts/one-time-sends/#daily-ramp).
---@field rate_limit_spread? boolean When `true`, spreads messages evenly across the time period. Otherwise, it sends as fast as possible up to the limit in each period.
---@field rate_limit_time_period? customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase0RateLimitTimePeriod|number Time period in seconds for rate limiting. Must be one of 60 (minute), 3600 (hour), or 86400 (day).
---@field recipient_file_url? string A URL pointing to a CSV of recipients, used instead of the `recipients` filter. Customer.io resolves the file in the background, so this request can't also send or schedule. Poll [Get a one-time send](/integrations/api/app/tag/newsletters/getNewsletters/) until `recipient_file_status` is `done`, then call [send](/integrations/api/app/tag/send-messages/sendNewsletter/) or [schedule](/integrations/api/app/tag/send-messages/scheduleNewsletter/).
---@field recipients? customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase0Recipients Filter conditions that define the one-time send's recipients. In `recipients`, you can combine `segment` and `attribute` conditions with `and`, `or`, and `not` operators. This endpoint enforces a strict shape: * The outermost object must be a single `and` array. * Every operator or condition object takes exactly **one** key: `and`, `or`, `not`, `segment`, or `attribute`. An object with two keys—like `not` alongside `and`—is rejected with an "Invalid filter spec" error. * Segment conditions must be wrapped in an `or` array, even for a single segment—and `or` arrays can contain only segment conditions. * To exclude segments, `not` must contain an `or` of segment conditions and sit as its own item inside the `and` array. * Attribute conditions sit directly in the `and` array, unwrapped. To negate an attribute condition, set `inverse: true` on the attribute itself—`not` can't contain attribute conditions. The email example on this operation shows or-wrapped segments combined with a negated attribute; for the common "include segment A, exclude segment B" pattern, see the **include one segment, exclude another** request example. See [Format API-triggered broadcasts](/messaging/send/broadcasts/api-triggered-data-format/#overriding-recipients) for general operator behavior.
---@field scheduled_at? number A Unix timestamp indicating when to send the one-time send. The time must be in the future. You cannot set both `send_now` and `scheduled_at`.
---@field send_now? boolean If `true`, the one-time send is sent immediately after creation. You cannot set both `send_now` and `scheduled_at`.
---@field subscription_topic_id? number The one-time send audience's subscription topic ID. Required when [subscription center](/journeys/channels/subscriptions/center/#enable-sub-center) is enabled; otherwise sends to globally subscribed profiles.
---@field tag_ids? customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase0TagIdsList The IDs of the tags you want to apply to the one-time send. Each tag must already exist.

---Time period in seconds for rate limiting. Must be one of 60 (minute), 3600 (hour), or 86400 (day).
---@alias customerio.CreateNewsletterRequestBodyCase0RateLimitTimePeriod 60|3600|86400

