---@alias customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseAction customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase0|customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase1|customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase2|customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase3

---@class customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase0
---@field bcc? string The blind-copy address(es) for this action.
---@field body? string The body of the action. You cannot modify the body if you created it with our drag-and-drop editor.
---@field body_amp? string AMP-enabled content for your email. If a recipient's email client doesn't support AMP, they receive your `body` content instead. Make sure you're [set up to send AMP](/journeys/channels/email/layouts/amp-for-email/) first.
---@field broadcast_id? number The identifier for a broadcast.
---@field campaign_id? number The identifier for an automation.
---@field cc? string The carbon-copy address(es) for this action.
---@field created? number The date time when the referenced ID was created.
---@field deduplicate_id? string An identifier in the format `id:timestamp` where the id is for the object you're working with (Automations, Deliveries, Exports, Identities, One-time sends, Segments, and Templates), and the timestamp is the last time the object was updated.
---@field fake_bcc? boolean If true, rather than sending true copies to BCC addresses, Customer.io sends a copy of the message with the subject line containing the recipient address(es).
---@field from? string The address that the message is from, relevant if the action `type` is `email`.
---@field from_id? number The identifier of the `from` address, commonly known as the "sender". Use [List sender identities](/integrations/api/app/tag/sender-identities/listSenders/) to find valid IDs.
---@field headers? string A JSON string containing header objects with `name` and `value`. Names and values must be strings, with no non-ASCII characters or spaces. You can't overwrite reserved headers.
---@field id? number The identifier for an action.
---@field language? string The language variant for your message. If you don't use our [localization feature](/journeys/channels/localization/getting-started), or this is the default message, this value is an empty string.
---@field layout? string The layout used for the action, if it exists.
---@field multi_language_branch_action_id? number Returned when the action is a language variant of a multi-language message. This id is the same for each variant of a message, so you can use this to retrieve metrics for a message and all its variants.
---@field name? string The name of the action, if it exists.
---@field parent_action_id? number The ID of the parent action, if the action occurred within an automation and has a parent (like a randomized split, etc).
---@field preheader_text? string [Also known as "preview text"](/journeys/channels/email/headers/custom-preheader-text/), this is the small block of text shown in an email inbox next to or underneath the subject line.
---@field preprocessor? customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase0Preprocessor If CSS pre-processing is enabled, this key is populated with `premailer`. Note, Juice replaced Premailer as the pre-processor, but you will only see `premailer` as the value.
---@field recipient? string The recipient address for an action.
---@field reply_to? string The address that receives replies for the message, if applicable.
---@field reply_to_id? number|distilled.Null The identifier for the `reply_to` address, if applicable. Use [List sender identities](/integrations/api/app/tag/sender-identities/listSenders/) to find valid IDs.
---@field sending_state? customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase0SendingState Determines the sending behavior for the action. `automatic` sends the action automatically when triggered; `draft` queues drafts when the action is triggered; or `off` to disable the action.
---@field subject? string The subject line for an `email` action.
---@field type? customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase0Type The type of action.
---@field updated? number The date time when the referenced ID was last updated.

---If CSS pre-processing is enabled, this key is populated with `premailer`. Note, Juice replaced Premailer as the pre-processor, but you will only see `premailer` as the value.
---@alias customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase0Preprocessor "premailer"

---Determines the sending behavior for the action. `automatic` sends the action automatically when triggered; `draft` queues drafts when the action is triggered; or `off` to disable the action.
---@alias customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase0SendingState "automatic"|"draft"|"off"

---The type of action.
---@alias customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase0Type "email"|"in_app"|"push"|"twilio"|"slack"|"whatsapp"

---@class customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase1
---@field body? string The body of your SMS.
---@field campaign_id? number The identifier for an automation.
---@field created? number The date time when the referenced ID was created.
---@field deduplicate_id? string An identifier in the format `id:timestamp` where the id is for the object you're working with (Automations, Deliveries, Exports, Identities, One-time sends, Segments, and Templates), and the timestamp is the last time the object was updated.
---@field id? number The identifier for an action.
---@field image_url? string The URL of the image in your SMS (MMS) message.
---@field language? string The language variant for your message. If you don't use our [localization feature](/journeys/channels/localization/getting-started), or this is the default message, this value is an empty string.
---@field layout? string The layout used for the action, if it exists.
---@field multi_language_branch_action_id? number Returned when the action is a language variant of a multi-language message. This id is the same for each variant of a message, so you can use this to retrieve metrics for a message and all its variants.
---@field name? string The name of the action.
---@field parent_action_id? number The ID of the parent action, if the action occurred within an automation and has a parent (like a randomized split, etc).
---@field recipient? string The recipient, usually an attribute you reference with Liquid like `{{customer.phone}}`. If you use Liquid, this field is blank in `GET` responses because we resolve the recipient at send time.
---@field sending_state? customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase1SendingState Determines the sending behavior for the action. `automatic` sends the action automatically when triggered; `draft` queues drafts when the action is triggered; or `off` to disable the action.
---@field type? customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase1Type For SMS/MMS messages, the `type` is always `twilio`.
---@field updated? number The date time when the referenced ID was last updated.

---Determines the sending behavior for the action. `automatic` sends the action automatically when triggered; `draft` queues drafts when the action is triggered; or `off` to disable the action.
---@alias customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase1SendingState "automatic"|"draft"|"off"

---For SMS/MMS messages, the `type` is always `twilio`.
---@alias customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase1Type "twilio"

---The action object for WhatsApp messages sent from Customer.io using your Facebook Business Account (not Twilio). Messages sent through Twilio still use the `twilio` type and are treated similarly to SMS messages.
---@class customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase2
---@field body? string A JSON string containing WhatsApp template metadata from Meta and template parameters with Liquid variables. Use `GET /v1/environments/{environment_id}/whatsapp/templates` to list templates.
---@field body_json? string For visual editor content (if applicable).
---@field campaign_id? number The identifier for an automation.
---@field created? number The date time when the referenced ID was created.
---@field deduplicate_id? string An identifier in the format `id:timestamp` where the id is for the object you're working with (Automations, Deliveries, Exports, Identities, One-time sends, Segments, and Templates), and the timestamp is the last time the object was updated.
---@field id? number The identifier for an action.
---@field language? string The language variant for your message. If you don't use our [localization feature](/journeys/channels/localization/getting-started), or this is the default message, this value is an empty string.
---@field multi_language_branch_action_id? number Returned when the action is a language variant of a multi-language message. This id is the same for each variant of a message, so you can use this to retrieve metrics for a message and all its variants.
---@field name? string The name of the action.
---@field parent_action_id? number The ID of the parent action, if the action occurred within an automation and has a parent (like a randomized split, etc).
---@field recipient? string The recipient's phone number in E.164 format, usually referenced with Liquid like `{{customer.phone}}`. If you use Liquid, this field is blank in `GET` responses because we resolve the recipient at send time.
---@field send_to_unsubscribed? boolean Whether to send this message to unsubscribed customers.
---@field sender_identity_id? number The ID of the WhatsApp Business phone number to send from. This corresponds to a phone number registered in your WhatsApp Business Account and synced via `GET /v1/environments/{environment_id}/whatsapp/sync`.
---@field sending_state? customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase2SendingState Determines the sending behavior for the action. `automatic` sends the action automatically when triggered; `draft` queues drafts when the action is triggered; or `off` to disable the action.
---@field tracked? boolean Whether links in template parameters should be tracked.
---@field type? customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase2Type For WhatsApp messages sent from Customer.io using your Facebook Business Account (not Twilio), the `type` is always `whatsapp`.
---@field updated? number The date time when the referenced ID was last updated.

---Determines the sending behavior for the action. `automatic` sends the action automatically when triggered; `draft` queues drafts when the action is triggered; or `off` to disable the action.
---@alias customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase2SendingState "automatic"|"draft"|"off"

---For WhatsApp messages sent from Customer.io using your Facebook Business Account (not Twilio), the `type` is always `whatsapp`.
---@alias customerio.GetCampaignActionResponseActionCase2Type "whatsapp"

