---@class customerio.GetCampaignMessagesRequest
---@field campaign_id number The ID of the automation that you want to trigger or return information about.
---@field start? string The token for the page of results you want to return. Responses contain a `next` property. Use this property as the `start` value to return the next page of results.
---@field limit? number The maximum number of results you want to retrieve per page.
---@field type? customerio.GetCampaignMessagesRequestType|string The type of item you want to return metrics for. When empty, the response contains metrics for all possible types.
---@field metric? customerio.GetCampaignMessagesRequestMetric|string Determines the metric(s) you want to return.
---@field drafts? boolean If true, your request returns drafts rather than active/sent messages.
---@field start_ts? number The beginning timestamp for your query.
---@field end_ts? number The ending timestamp for your query.
---@field get_tracked_responses? boolean If true, the response includes `tracked_responses` for each message—an object containing tracked response option names for in-app survey responses.

---@alias customerio.GetCampaignMessagesRequestMetric "attempted"|"sent"|"delivered"|"opened"|"clicked"|"converted"|"bounced"|"spammed"|"unsubscribed"|"dropped"|"failed"|"undeliverable"

---@alias customerio.GetCampaignMessagesRequestType "email"|"webhook"|"twilio"|"whatsapp"|"slack"|"push"|"in_app"|"live_notification"

---@class customerio.GetCampaignMessagesResponse
---@field messages? customerio.GetCampaignMessagesResponseMessagesList

---Describes an individual message delivery. The object contains keys for all possible parents of the message (`newsletter_id`, `broadcast_id`, etc) but only the parents of the delivery are populated. Other parent IDs are null.
---@class customerio.GetCampaignMessagesResponseMessagesItem
---@field action_id? number The identifier for an action.
---@field broadcast_id? number|distilled.Null
---@field campaign_id? number|distilled.Null
---@field content_id? number The identifier for a message in a one-time send. One-time sends can have multiple content IDs (for multi-language messages or A/B tests).
---@field created? number The date time when the referenced ID was created.
---@field customer_id? string|distilled.Null The ID of a customer profile, analogous to a "person" in the UI. If your workspace supports multiple identifiers (email and ID), this value can be null.
---@field customer_identifiers? customerio.GetCampaignMessagesResponseMessagesItemCustomerIdentifiers Identifiers for the person in a response—`id`, `cio_id`, and `email`. Unset `id` or `email` values are `null`. We recommend this object over the less descriptive `customer_id`. This object doesn't include `phone`, even if your workspace uses phone numbers as an identifier; look for the person's `phone` attribute instead.
---@field deduplicate_id? string An identifier in the format `id:timestamp` where the id is for the object you're working with (Automations, Deliveries, Exports, Identities, One-time sends, Segments, and Templates), and the timestamp is the last time the object was updated.
---@field failure_message? string|distilled.Null Explains why a message failed, if applicable.
---@field forgotten? boolean If true message contents are not retained by Customer.io.
---@field id? string The identifier for a delivery—the instance of a message intended for an individual recipient.
---@field message_template_id? number The identifier of the message template used to create a message.
---@field metrics? customerio.GetCampaignMessagesResponseMessagesItemMetrics Metrics for an individual instance of a message; each item in the object represents the timestamp when a message achieved a particular metric. This object only contains metrics that have been recorded.
---@field newsletter_id? number|distilled.Null
---@field parent_action_id? number The ID of the parent action, if the action occurred within an automation and has a parent (like a randomized split, etc).
---@field recipient? string The recipient address for an action.
---@field subject? string The subject line for an `email` action.
---@field tracked_responses? customerio.GetCampaignMessagesResponseMessagesItemTrackedResponsesMap Tracked in-app survey responses, keyed by response option name. Present only when `get_tracked_responses` is `true`.
---@field trigger_event_id? string The id of the event that triggered an event-triggered automation (not an API-triggered broadcast).
---@field type? customerio.GetCampaignMessagesResponseMessagesItemType The type of message or action for a delivery, automation action, or related object. Includes channels that one-time sends do not support (for example, `slack` and `whatsapp`).

