---@class customerio.GetCollectionWriteRequest
---@field collection_id number The identifier for a collection.
---@field write_id string The `id` that Customer.io returned when you submitted the write request.

---@class customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponse
---@field write? customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWrite

---@class customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWrite
---@field code? customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWriteCode If the write request's `state` is `failed`, the code explains why. A write of up to 500 rows saves nothing when it fails, and a larger write keeps the rows it saved before it failed. `source-refused` means Customer.io couldn't download the file, or the source is gone or unusable. `replace-unfinished` means an earlier replacement stopped partway, so you need to replace the collection's rows again.
---@field id? string The identifier for the write request. Use it to look up the write's status.
---@field items? customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWriteItemsList For a write request that failed with `items`, up to 500 of the rows that Customer.io rejected. Customer.io didn't save any of the rows.
---@field message? string A readable explanation of the failure.
---@field state? customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWriteState Where the write request stands. `replaced` means that a later replacement of the whole collection ran first, so the collection ends up as if this write ran before the replacement.

---If the write request's `state` is `failed`, the code explains why. A write of up to 500 rows saves nothing when it fails, and a larger write keeps the rows it saved before it failed. `source-refused` means Customer.io couldn't download the file, or the source is gone or unusable. `replace-unfinished` means an earlier replacement stopped partway, so you need to replace the collection's rows again.
---@alias customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWriteCode "storage-limit-reached"|"too-large"|"invalid-data"|"no-key-field"|"delete-field-is-key"|"items"|"source-unauthorized"|"superseded"|"expired"|"canceled"|"collection-not-found"|"source-refused"|"replace-unfinished"

---@class customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWriteItemsItem
---@field code? customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWriteItemsItemCode Why the row failed.
---@field index? number The row's position in the write request, starting at 0. For a write that sends `data`, this is the row's position in the `data` array. For a write from a file, this is the row's position among the file's rows.
---@field key? string The row's key, if it has one.

---Why the row failed.
---@alias customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWriteItemsItemCode "missing-key"|"duplicate-key"|"key-too-long"|"key-field-repeated"|"field-too-long"|"not-an-object"

---For a write request that failed with `items`, up to 500 of the rows that Customer.io rejected. Customer.io didn't save any of the rows.
---@alias customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWriteItemsList customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWriteItemsItem[]

---Where the write request stands. `replaced` means that a later replacement of the whole collection ran first, so the collection ends up as if this write ran before the replacement.
---@alias customerio.GetCollectionWriteResponseWriteState "queued"|"applied"|"replaced"|"failed"

