---The profile you referenced by ID in the request.
---@class customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomer
---@field attributes? customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerAttributes Contains attributes assigned to this profile, including your workspace's people-identifiers (by default, these are `id`, `email`, and `cio_id`). Attributes are all stored as strings.
---@field devices? customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerDevicesList Lists the devices associated with the customer profile.
---@field id? string The customer ID referenced in the request.
---@field identifiers? customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerIdentifiers Identifiers for the person in a response—`id`, `cio_id`, and `email`. Unset `id` or `email` values are `null`. We recommend this object over the less descriptive `customer_id`. This object doesn't include `phone`, even if your workspace uses phone numbers as an identifier; look for the person's `phone` attribute instead.
---@field timestamps? customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerTimestamps The epoch timestamps when corresponding attributes were set on the customer profile.
---@field unsubscribed? boolean If `true`, a person is globally unsubscribed from email, SMS, WhatsApp, and push. Values like `true`, `TRUE`, `1`, and `"1"` count as true; other values are treated as subscribed or topic-based.

---Contains attributes assigned to this profile, including your workspace's people-identifiers (by default, these are `id`, `email`, and `cio_id`). Attributes are all stored as strings.
---@class customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerAttributes
---@field _cio_subscription_preferences_computed? string A person's computed subscription preferences as stringified JSON, combining set preferences with defaults for unset topics. [Learn more about backfilled preferences](/messaging/channels/subscriptions/center/#backfill-preferences).
---@field cio_id? string A unique identifier set by Customer.io, used to reference a person if you want to update their identifiers.
---@field cio_subscription_preferences? string A person's subscription preferences as stringified JSON. If unset, preferences are computed from topic defaults; see `_cio_subscription_preferences_computed`.
---@field email? string|distilled.Null The email address of the customer.
---@field id? string|distilled.Null The ID of a customer profile, analogous to a "person" in the UI. If your workspace supports multiple identifiers (email and ID), this value can be null.
---@field [string] any

---Device properties collected by [Customer.io SDKs](/integrations/sdk/) unless `autoTrackDeviceAttributes` is disabled. You can use these properties in segments and Liquid.
---@class customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerDevicesItem
---@field id string The unique device identifier. This is an APNs token, an FCM registration token, or a [Firebase Installation ID (FID)](/messaging/channels/push/developer-guide/#device-ids).
---@field platform customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerDevicesItemPlatform The device/messaging platform.
---@field attributes? customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerDevicesItemAttributes Attributes that you can reference to segment your audience—like a person's attributes, but specific to a device. These can be either the attributes defined below or custom key-value attributes.
---@field last_used? number The `timestamp` when you last identified this device. If you don't pass a timestamp when you add or update a device, we use the time of the request itself. Our SDKs identify a device when a person launches their app.
---@field token_type? customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerDevicesItemTokenType Used with FCM. This represents the kind of ID in the device's `id` field, either `fid` for a [Firebase Installation ID](/messaging/channels/push/developer-guide/#device-ids) or `token` for an FCM registration token. This field is not used with APNs. See [Token types](/messaging/channels/push/developer-guide/#token-types) to learn how Customer.io supports each kind of ID.

---Attributes that you can reference to segment your audience—like a person's attributes, but specific to a device. These can be either the attributes defined below or custom key-value attributes.
---@class customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerDevicesItemAttributes
---@field _last_status? customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerDevicesItemAttributesLastStatus The delivery status of the last message sent to the device—sent, bounced, or suppressed. An empty string indicates that that the device hasn't received a push yet.
---@field app_identifier? string The app that the device belongs to—the **Bundle ID / App identifier** you entered with that app's push credentials. If you have more than one app, we use this attribute to send push notifications to the right app. A device without an app identifier receives push notifications you send to your [default app](/messaging/channels/push/getting-started/#the-default-app).
---@field app_version? string The version of your app that a customer uses. You might target app versions to let people know when they need to update, or expose them to new features when they do.
---@field cio_sdk_version? string The version of the Customer.io SDK in the app.
---@field device_locale? string The device's [IETF language code](/journeys/channels/localization/getting-started/#supported-languages), such as `en-MX` or `es-ES`.
---@field device_model? string The model of the device a person uses.
---@field device_os? string The operating system, including the version, on the device.
---@field push_enabled? customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerDevicesItemAttributesPushEnabled If `"true"`, the device is opted-in and can receive push notifications.
---@field [string] any

---The delivery status of the last message sent to the device—sent, bounced, or suppressed. An empty string indicates that that the device hasn't received a push yet.
---@alias customerio.GetPersonAttributesResponseCustomerDevicesItemAttributesLastStatus ""|"bounced"|"sent"|"suppressed"

