---@field conditions? customerio.GetSegmentResponseSegmentConditionsMap The conditions that determine who belongs to the segment, as a tree of nested `and` and `or` groups. Customer.io includes this object for data-driven and snapshot segments and omits it for manual segments, which don't have conditions. A profile attribute condition appears as an `attribute_change` event with a `to` filter and an inverted `from` filter, and filter values are always strings, even for numeric or boolean attributes.
---@field created_at? number The date time when the referenced ID was created.
---@field deduplicate_id? string An identifier in the format `id:timestamp` where the id is for the object you're working with (Automations, Deliveries, Exports, Identities, One-time sends, Segments, and Templates), and the timestamp is the last time the object was updated.
