---@field id? number The identifier for a segment; used to target a segment in requests.
---@field name? string The name of the segment.
---@field progress? number|distilled.Null Customer.io returns `0` while the segment is in the `build` state and `null` when it's `finished`. This field doesn't report partial progress, so use `state` to tell whether the segment is still building.
---@field state? customerio.GetSegmentResponseSegmentState The segment's build state. The state is `build` while Customer.io calculates who belongs to the segment, and `finished` when membership is up to date.
---@field tags? customerio.GetSegmentResponseSegmentTagsList|distilled.Null The tags assigned to the segment, if any. Tags may help you sort through your segments.
---@field type? customerio.GetSegmentResponseSegmentType The type of segment. [Learn more in our segmentation docs.](/messaging/segmentation/segments/#types-of-segments)
---@field updated_at? number The date time when the referenced ID was last updated.

