---@class customerio.GetWebhookRequest
---@field webhook_id number The identifier of a webhook.

---@class customerio.GetWebhookResponse
---@field endpoint string The webhook URL.
---@field events customerio.GetWebhookResponseEventsList Specifies the types of events you want to report to your webhook. See our [reporting webhooks reference](/integrations/api/webhooks/) for more information about event types and the information they return.
---@field name string The name of your webhook.
---@field disabled? boolean Set to `true` to quit sending events to the webhook URL. Set to `false` to enable the webhook.
---@field full_resolution? boolean Set to `false` to send unique open and click events to the webhook. Set to `true` to send all events.
---@field id? number The identifier for the webhook.
---@field type? customerio.GetWebhookResponseType The type of webhook—`webhook` for a standard reporting webhook or `js` for a JavaScript webhook.
---@field with_content? boolean Set to `true` to include message content in `sent` events and topic preferences in `cio_subscription_preferences_changed` events. This is the **Body content** option in the UI.

