---Contains your import parameters for adding or updating geofences in a geofence set.
---@class customerio.ImportRequestImportCase4
---@field data_file_url string The URL of the CSV, GeoJSON, or GeoJSONL file of geofences you want to import. Customer.io reads the file as GeoJSON when its name ends in `.geojson`, `.geojsonl`, or `.json`, or when its content starts with `{`, and as CSV otherwise.
---@field geoset_id string The ID of the geofence set you want to import geofences into. The set must already exist in your workspace. Customer.io doesn't check the set when it accepts your request, so a request with an ID that doesn't match a set still succeeds, and the import fails afterward with an error that the geoset doesn't exist. [Look up the import](/integrations/api/app/tag/imports/getImport/) to confirm that it succeeded.
---@field name string A friendly name for your import. This helps you identify your import.
---@field type customerio.ImportRequestImportCase4Type|string The type of import.
---@field description? string A helpful description that can help you find and recognize your import operation.
---@field geoset_mode? customerio.ImportRequestImportCase4GeosetMode|string How the import treats geofences that are already in the set. `merge` adds new geofences and updates existing ones. `replace` replaces all the geofences already in the set with the ones you import. In both modes, a geofence with an `external_id` that matches an existing geofence updates that geofence in every set it belongs to.

---How the import treats geofences that are already in the set. `merge` adds new geofences and updates existing ones. `replace` replaces all the geofences already in the set with the ones you import. In both modes, a geofence with an `external_id` that matches an existing geofence updates that geofence in every set it belongs to.
---@alias customerio.ImportRequestImportCase4GeosetMode "merge"|"replace"

---The type of import.
---@alias customerio.ImportRequestImportCase4Type "geoset"

