---@class customerio.ListActivitiesRequest
---@field start? string The token for the page of results you want to return. Responses contain a `next` property. Use this property as the `start` value to return the next page of results.
---@field type? customerio.ListActivitiesRequestType|string The type of activity you want to search for. Types with `_o:<object_type_id>` are for objects and types with `_r:<object_type_id>` are for relationships.
---@field name? string The name of the event or attribute you want to return. For `consent` activities, the consent action, like `opted_in` or `opted_out`.
---@field deleted? boolean If true, return results for deleted people.
---@field customer_id? string The `identifier` of the person you want to look up. By default, this is a person's `id`. You can use the `id_type` parameter to look up a person by `email`, `phone`, or `cio_id`. If you use a person's `cio_id`, you must prefix the value with `cio_` when using it to find or reference a person (i.e. `cio_03000010` for a `cio_id` value of 03000010).
