---@class customerio.SendNewsletterRequest
---@field newsletter_id number The identifier of a one-time send.
---@field expires_after? number A send window in seconds measured from the moment the send starts, or `0` for no expiry. Customer.io stops delivering the one-time send once the window closes. You can't combine it with send time optimization, and on an A/B test it must outlast the test duration.
---@field rate_limit_email_rate? number Maximum number of messages per time period. **NOTE:** Though this states `email_rate`, you can use this for other message channels. Only fixed rate limits are supported, not [daily ramp limits](/messaging/send/broadcasts/one-time-sends/#daily-ramp).
---@field rate_limit_spread? boolean When `true`, spreads messages evenly across the time period. Otherwise, it sends as fast as possible up to the limit in each period.
---@field rate_limit_time_period? customerio.SendNewsletterRequestRateLimitTimePeriod|number Time period in seconds for rate limiting. Must be one of 60 (minute), 3600 (hour), or 86400 (day).

