---@class customerio.SendNewsletterResponse
---@field newsletter? customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletter

---@class customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletter
---@field content_ids? customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterContentIdsList A list of message variants in a one-time send, where a variant is a translation or A/B test.
---@field created? number The date time when the referenced ID was created.
---@field deduplicate_id? string An identifier in the format `id:timestamp` where the id is for the object you're working with (Automations, Deliveries, Exports, Identities, One-time sends, Segments, and Templates), and the timestamp is the last time the object was updated.
---@field expires_after? number The send window in seconds, if you set one. Customer.io stops delivering the one-time send this long after it starts.
---@field id? number The identifier for a one-time send.
---@field name? string The name of the one-time send. Must be 190 characters or less.
---@field recipient_file_error? string Why the recipient file failed, when `recipient_file_status` is `error`. Customer.io omits it otherwise.
---@field recipient_file_status? customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterRecipientFileStatus How far Customer.io has got with a recipient file, whether you uploaded it in the UI or passed `recipient_file_url`. Customer.io omits this field when the audience came from a `recipients` filter. Wait for `done` before you send or schedule.
---@field recipient_segment_ids? customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterRecipientSegmentIdsList If the recipient conditions included segments, this returns a list of those segment ids.
---@field scheduled_at? number|distilled.Null When the one-time send is scheduled to go out, or `null` if it has no active schedule. Always included. - A paused one-time send keeps its schedule, so this still has a value while `send_state` is `paused`. - After sending starts, this stores the next scheduled send if there is one, like the next timezone batch or the remainder of an A/B test. - When `tz_match_enabled` is `true`, the `scheduled_at` property is the time you asked for in the [schedule request](/integrations/api/app/tag/send-messages/scheduleNewsletter/) until sending starts. - If you send immediately instead of scheduling, there's a short delay before Customer.io starts sending. During that delay, `scheduled_at` isn't `null` and isn't a future time: it's the time you made the request, an earlier time, or `0`. - While Customer.io [holds the send](/messaging/send/broadcasts/one-time-sends/#queued-sends) until its segments finish building, this is the next time Customer.io checks the segments.
---@field send_state? customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterSendState Where the one-time send is in its lifecycle. Always included. This matches the status shown in Customer.io, with one exception noted under `awaiting_winner`. - `drafted`: The one-time send isn't scheduled and hasn't been sent. - `scheduled`: A send time is set and sending hasn't started. A scheduled send that Customer.io is holding until its segments finish building also reports `scheduled`. - `sending`: Sending has started and is still in progress. More batches are due (timezone-match batches or the remainder of an A/B test), or messages are still being delivered. A send-now send that Customer.io is holding until its segments finish building also reports `sending`. - `sent`: The one-time send is no longer sending. This doesn't mean that every individual message has reached a final state. - `paused`: The one-time send is paused. - `stopped`: The one-time send was stopped. - `failed`: The one-time send failed. - `awaiting_winner`: An A/B test has started and is waiting for you to pick a winner before the rest of the audience gets it. Test messages might still be going out. Customer.io's UI stops showing "awaiting winner" 30 days after the first send, but the API keeps reporting `awaiting_winner` because you can still pick a winner. When more than one state applies, Customer.io reports the first match in this order: `stopped`, `failed`, `paused`, `awaiting_winner`, `sending`, `sent`, `scheduled`, `drafted`.
---@field sent_at? number|distilled.Null The last time the one-time send was sent, or `null` if it hasn't been sent.
---@field subscription_topic_id? number If you enabled a [subscription center](/journeys/channels/subscriptions/center/) on your workspace, this returns the id of the subscription preference you set.
---@field tags? customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterTagsList An array of tags associated with the one-time send.
---@field timezone? string The [IANA timezone name](/journeys/send/timezones/example-timezones/#region-format) of the schedule (for example, `America/New_York`). Customer.io includes this field only when the active schedule has a timezone. It's omitted otherwise.
---@field type? customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterType Channel type for a one-time send or one-time send content variant.
---@field tz_match_enabled? boolean `true` when the pending schedule sends at the same local time in each person's timezone. Customer.io includes this field only while a timezone-match schedule is pending. It's omitted otherwise and is never `false`.
---@field updated? number The date time when the referenced ID was last updated.

---A list of message variants in a one-time send, where a variant is a translation or A/B test.
---@alias customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterContentIdsList number[]

---How far Customer.io has got with a recipient file, whether you uploaded it in the UI or passed `recipient_file_url`. Customer.io omits this field when the audience came from a `recipients` filter. Wait for `done` before you send or schedule.
---@alias customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterRecipientFileStatus "pending"|"processing"|"done"|"error"

---If the recipient conditions included segments, this returns a list of those segment ids.
---@alias customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterRecipientSegmentIdsList number[]

---Where the one-time send is in its lifecycle. Always included. This matches the status shown in Customer.io, with one exception noted under `awaiting_winner`.
---
---- `drafted`: The one-time send isn't scheduled and hasn't been sent.
---- `scheduled`: A send time is set and sending hasn't started. A scheduled send that Customer.io is holding until its segments finish building also reports `scheduled`.
---- `sending`: Sending has started and is still in progress. More batches are due (timezone-match batches or the remainder of an A/B test), or messages are still being delivered. A send-now send that Customer.io is holding until its segments finish building also reports `sending`.
---- `sent`: The one-time send is no longer sending. This doesn't mean that every individual message has reached a final state.
---- `paused`: The one-time send is paused.
---- `stopped`: The one-time send was stopped.
---- `failed`: The one-time send failed.
---- `awaiting_winner`: An A/B test has started and is waiting for you to pick a winner before the rest of the audience gets it. Test messages might still be going out. Customer.io's UI stops showing "awaiting winner" 30 days after the first send, but the API keeps reporting `awaiting_winner` because you can still pick a winner.
---
---When more than one state applies, Customer.io reports the first match in this order: `stopped`, `failed`, `paused`, `awaiting_winner`, `sending`, `sent`, `scheduled`, `drafted`.
---@alias customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterSendState "drafted"|"scheduled"|"sending"|"sent"|"paused"|"stopped"|"failed"|"awaiting_winner"

---An array of tags associated with the one-time send.
---@alias customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterTagsList string[]

---Channel type for a one-time send or one-time send content variant.
---@alias customerio.SendNewsletterResponseNewsletterType "email"|"webhook"|"twilio"|"push"|"in_app"|"inbox"

---@class customerio.SendPushRequest
---@field identifiers customerio.SendPushRequestIdentifiers Identifies the person represented by your transactional message by one of, and only one of, `id`, `email`, or `cio_id`.
---@field transactional_message_id customerio.SendPushRequestTransactionalMessageId The transactional message template that you want to use for your message. You can call the template by its numerical ID or by the *Trigger Name* that you assigned to the template in the UI (case insensitive).
---@field auto_create? boolean If `true` and your `transactional_message_id` doesn't match a record, Customer.io creates an empty record using that value as the *Trigger Name*. The ID must be a string. If the name already belongs to another channel, the request fails with `400`, and numeric IDs ignore this setting. See [details](/journeys/transactional-email/#auto-create-transactional-message-records).
---@field custom_data? any Optional key/value pairs you want to attach to the push payload. Firebase only supports string values. This overrides the Custom Data from your transactional template.
---@field custom_device? customerio.SendPushRequestCustomDevice A device to perform an upsert operation at the time of send. The device will be added/updated on the profile from the Identifiers block.
---@field custom_payload? customerio.SendPushRequestCustomPayload Optional key/value pairs you want to attach to the push payload. Firebase only supports string values. This overrides all other payload values, including the Custom Payload from your transactional template.
---@field disable_message_retention? boolean If true, the message body is not retained in delivery history. Setting this value overrides the value set in the settings of your `transactional_message_id`.
---@field image_url? string An image URL to show in the push. This overrides Image from the transactional template (referenced by `transactional_message_id`).
---@field language? string Overrides language preferences for the person you want to send your transactional message to. Use one of our [supported two- or four-letter language codes](/journeys/channels/localization/getting-started/#supported-languages).
---@field link? string A deep link to open when the push is tapped. This overrides Link from the transactional template (referenced by `transactional_message_id`).
---@field message? string The message body for your notification. This overrides the notification body of the transactional template (referenced by `transactional_message_id`).
---@field message_data? customerio.SendPushRequestMessageDataMap An object containing the key-value pairs referenced using liquid in your message.
---@field platform? customerio.SendPushRequestPlatform|string The devices this send goes to, overriding the platform saved on the transactional message for this request only. `all` is iOS and Android, `web` is browsers only, and `all_and_web` is iOS, Android, and browsers. If you leave it out, the send uses the message's platform; with `auto_create`, a new message keeps the platform of its first request. Values other than `all` require [web push](/messaging/channels/web-push/transactional/) for your account; without it, the request fails with `400`.
---@field queue_draft? boolean If true, your transactional message is held as a draft in Customer.io and not sent directly to your audience. You must go to the Deliveries and Drafts page to send your message.
---@field send_at? number A unix timestamp (seconds since epoch) determining when the message will be sent. The timestamp can be up to 90 days in the future. If this value is in the past, your message is sent immediately.
---@field send_to_unsubscribed? boolean If false, your message is not sent to unsubscribed recipients. Setting this value overrides the value set in the settings of your `transactional_message_id`.
---@field sound? customerio.SendPushRequestSound|string **For iOS Only**: your notification can alert users with the device's default notification sound or play no sound at all.
---@field title? string The title for your notification. This overrides the title of the transactional template (referenced by `transactional_message_id`).
---@field to? customerio.SendPushRequestTo|string The devices you want to send this push to—`all`, `last_used`, or a custom device token from the identified profile. Defaults to `all` and overrides the `To` value from your transactional template.

---A device to perform an upsert operation at the time of send. The device will be added/updated on the profile from the Identifiers block.
---@class customerio.SendPushRequestCustomDevice
---@field platform customerio.SendPushRequestCustomDevicePlatform|string The device/messaging platform.
---@field token string The device token.
---@field attributes? customerio.SendPushRequestCustomDeviceAttributes Attributes that you can reference to segment your audience—like a person's attributes, but specific to a device. These can be either the attributes defined below or custom key-value attributes.
---@field last_used? number The `timestamp` when you last identified this device. If you don't pass a timestamp when you add or update a device, we use the time of the request itself. Our SDKs identify a device when a person launches their app.

---Attributes that you can reference to segment your audience—like a person's attributes, but specific to a device. These can be either the attributes defined below or custom key-value attributes.
