---@class customerio.StartLiveNotificationRequest
---@field attributes customerio.StartLiveNotificationRequestAttributes Static fields used to create the activity—an order number, a flight's origin and destination, or the teams in a match. On iOS they can't change after start. On Android, include the static fields your renderer needs on update and end calls too, because the SDK renders from a merged payload. The shape depends on your `notification_type`: pick the free form variant for iOS or a free form Android activity, or the matching bundled-template variant below. Template fields are documented for [iOS](/integrations/sdk/ios/live-activities/reference/#built-in-templates) and [Android](/integrations/sdk/android/live-notifications/reference/#built-in-templates).
---@field content_state customerio.StartLiveNotificationRequestContentState The initial dynamic content for the activity—the status, score, or ETA the device renders. Send the complete state on every call; partial updates aren't supported. The shape depends on your `notification_type`: pick the free form variant for iOS or a free form Android activity, or the matching bundled-template variant below. Date fields are epoch seconds.
---@field identifiers customerio.StartLiveNotificationRequestIdentifiers Identifies the profile you want to start the activity for. You must provide exactly one of `id`, `email`, `phone`, or `internal` (our internal identifier, `cio_` followed by an alphanumeric string). You cannot target anonymous profiles.
---@field notification_type string The reverse-DNS identifier of the activity type, like `io.customer.livenotifications.segments`. Must match a type your app registered with the SDK.
---@field app_identifier? string The identifier of the app to start the activity on—a bundle ID on iOS or a package name on Android. This only matters when your workspace has multiple apps: set it to target a device belonging to that app, or omit it to target the workspace's default app. Workspaces without multiple apps ignore this field. If you provide a value that doesn't match an app in your workspace, the request fails with a `400`.
---@field deep_link? string A link to open when the person taps the activity.
---@field device_id? string The device token identifying the device to start the activity on.
---@field expiration? number A unix timestamp (in seconds) for when the activity should expire. Must be no more than 6 hours in the future—values outside the range between now and that 6-hour maximum are rejected with a `400`. If you omit it (or pass `0`), the activity expires 6 hours after it starts.
---@field platform? customerio.StartLiveNotificationRequestPlatform|string The device platform.
---@field push_payload? customerio.StartLiveNotificationRequestPushPayload The alert shown when the activity starts. Required for iOS.

---Static fields used to create the activity—an order number, a flight's origin and destination, or the teams in a match. On iOS they can't change after start. On Android, include the static fields your renderer needs on update and end calls too, because the SDK renders from a merged payload. The shape depends on your `notification_type`: pick the free form variant for iOS or a free form Android activity, or the matching bundled-template variant below. Template fields are documented for [iOS](/integrations/sdk/ios/live-activities/reference/#built-in-templates) and [Android](/integrations/sdk/android/live-notifications/reference/#built-in-templates).
---@alias customerio.StartLiveNotificationRequestAttributes customerio.StartLiveNotificationRequestAttributesCase0Map|customerio.StartLiveNotificationRequestAttributesCase1|customerio.StartLiveNotificationRequestAttributesCase2

