---@class customerio.SubmitCollectionWriteRequestBodyCase1
---@field url string The `http` or `https` URL of your CSV or JSON file, like a signed URL to a file in your own storage. Customer.io detects the format from the `Content-Type` that your URL returns, or from the file extension if the `Content-Type` doesn't say. JSON data can be an array of objects or one object per line. CSV data needs a header row, and Customer.io reads every CSV value as a string. A file can be up to 500 MB and 1,000,000 rows.

---@class customerio.SubmitCollectionWriteRequestBodyCase2
---@field path string The file's path, relative to the source's `prefix`, like `daily/products.csv`. Use forward slashes. The path can't leave the prefix, so it can't contain `..` or `\`. Customer.io reads the file the same way it reads a file from a `url`.
---@field source_id string The `id` of the [collection source](/integrations/api/app/tag/collections/createCollectionSource/) that holds the file.

---@class customerio.SubmitCollectionWriteResponse

---@class customerio.TransactionalLinksRequest
---@field transactional_id number The identifier of your transactional message. You'll find this in the UI or URL of your transactional message. For example, if this is the path of a transactional message URL - `/transactional/3/templates/139` - the `transactional_id` is 3.
---@field period? customerio.TransactionalLinksRequestPeriod|string The unit of time for your report.
---@field steps? number The number of periods you want to return. Defaults to the maximum available, or `12` if the period is in `months`. Maximums are 24 hours, 45 days, 12 weeks, or 121 months. Days start at 00:00 EST. Weeks start at 00:00 EST on Sunday. Months start at 00:00 EST on the 1st of the month.
---@field unique? boolean If true, the response contains only unique customer results, i.e. a customer who clicks a link twice is only counted once. If false, the response contains the total number of results without regard to uniqueness.

---@alias customerio.TransactionalLinksRequestPeriod "hours"|"days"|"weeks"|"months"

