---@field created? number The date time when the referenced ID was created.
---@field customer_id? string|distilled.Null The ID of a customer profile, analogous to a "person" in the UI. If your workspace supports multiple identifiers (email and ID), this value can be null.
---@field customer_identifiers? customerio.TransactionalMessagesResponseMessagesItemCustomerIdentifiers Identifiers for the person in a response—`id`, `cio_id`, and `email`. Unset `id` or `email` values are `null`. We recommend this object over the less descriptive `customer_id`. This object doesn't include `phone`, even if your workspace uses phone numbers as an identifier; look for the person's `phone` attribute instead.
---@field deduplicate_id? string An identifier in the format `id:timestamp` where the id is for the object you're working with (Automations, Deliveries, Exports, Identities, One-time sends, Segments, and Templates), and the timestamp is the last time the object was updated.
---@field failure_message? string|distilled.Null Explains why a message failed, if applicable.
---@field forgotten? boolean If true message contents are not retained by Customer.io.
---@field id? string The identifier for a delivery—the instance of a message intended for an individual recipient.
---@field message_template_id? number The identifier of the message template used to create a message.
---@field metrics? customerio.TransactionalMessagesResponseMessagesItemMetrics Metrics for an individual instance of a message; each item in the object represents the timestamp when a message achieved a particular metric. This object only contains metrics that have been recorded.
---@field newsletter_id? number|distilled.Null
---@field parent_action_id? number The ID of the parent action, if the action occurred within an automation and has a parent (like a randomized split, etc).
---@field recipient? string The recipient address for an action.
---@field subject? string The subject line for an `email` action.
---@field tracked_responses? customerio.TransactionalMessagesResponseMessagesItemTrackedResponsesMap Tracked in-app survey responses, keyed by response option name. Present only when `get_tracked_responses` is `true`.
---@field trigger_event_id? string The id of the event that triggered an event-triggered automation (not an API-triggered broadcast).
---@field type? customerio.TransactionalMessagesResponseMessagesItemType The type of message or action for a delivery, automation action, or related object. Includes channels that one-time sends do not support (for example, `slack` and `whatsapp`).

---Identifiers for the person in a response—`id`, `cio_id`, and `email`. Unset `id` or `email` values are `null`. We recommend this object over the less descriptive `customer_id`. This object doesn't include `phone`, even if your workspace uses phone numbers as an identifier; look for the person's `phone` attribute instead.
---@class customerio.TransactionalMessagesResponseMessagesItemCustomerIdentifiers
---@field cio_id string A unique identifier set by Customer.io, used to reference a person if you want to update their identifiers.
---@field email string|distilled.Null A person's email address, if set.
---@field id string|distilled.Null A person's unique ID, if set. This is the same as the `customer_id` if present.

---Metrics for an individual instance of a message; each item in the object represents the timestamp when a message achieved a particular metric. This object only contains metrics that have been recorded.
---@class customerio.TransactionalMessagesResponseMessagesItemMetrics
---@field bounced? number The timestamp when the message `bounced`.
---@field clicked? number The timestamp when the message was `clicked`.
---@field converted? number The timestamp when the message was `converted`.
---@field created? number The timestamp when the message was `created`.
---@field delivered? number The timestamp when the message was `delivered`.
---@field drafted? number The timestamp when the message was `drafted`.
---@field dropped? number The timestamp when the message was `dropped`.
---@field failed? number The timestamp when the message `failed`.
---@field human_clicked? number The number of `clicked` messages excluding machine clicks. This metric is reliable starting April 20, 2025. [Learn more](/messaging/metrics/analytics/#delivery-metrics).
---@field human_opened? number The number of `opened` messages excluding machine opens. This metric is reliable starting March 20, 2025. [Learn more](/messaging/metrics/analytics/#delivery-metrics).
---@field opened? number The timestamp when the message was `opened`.
---@field prefetch_clicked? number The number of `clicked` messages attributed to machines. This metric is reliable starting April 20, 2025.
---@field prefetch_opened? number The number of `opened` messages attributed to machines. This metric is reliable starting March 20, 2025.
---@field sent? number The timestamp when the message was `sent`.
---@field spammed? number The timestamp when the message was marked as spam.
---@field undeliverable? number The timestamp when the message became `undeliverable`.
---@field unsubscribed? number The timestamp when a person unsubscribed based on this message.

---Tracked in-app survey responses, keyed by response option name. Present only when `get_tracked_responses` is `true`.
---@alias customerio.TransactionalMessagesResponseMessagesItemTrackedResponsesMap { [string]: customerio.TransactionalMessagesResponseMessagesItemTrackedResponsesValue }

---@class customerio.TransactionalMessagesResponseMessagesItemTrackedResponsesValue
---@field id? number The identifier for the tracked response.
---@field ts? number A unix timestamp representing when the response was tracked.

---The type of message or action for a delivery, automation action, or related object. Includes channels that one-time sends do not support (for example, `slack` and `whatsapp`).
