---@class customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequest
---@field broadcast_id number The ID of the broadcast that you want to trigger.
---@field body? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBody

---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBody customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase0|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase2|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase3|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase4|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase5

---Send your broadcast to the default set of recipients defined in the UI.
---@class customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase0
---@field data? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase0DataMap Contains information you want to use to populate your broadcast.
---@field email_add_duplicates? boolean an email address associated with more than one profile id is an error.
---@field email_ignore_missing? boolean If false, a missing email causes the broadcast to error and fail. If true, the broadcast will skip over any people in your audience who don't have emails, and continue sending to the rest of your audience.
---@field expires_after? number Number of seconds after the send starts that the broadcast should stop sending. Omit or set to `0` if you don't want the broadcast to expire. A rate-limited send always expires: if you set `rate_limit` and omit this field or set it to `0`, we set it to 30 days. If the broadcast expires before it finishes sending, Customer.io discards the messages that haven't gone out yet instead of delivering them late. The window runs from `scheduled_at` when you schedule the send, and from the time we receive this request when you don't.
---@field id_ignore_missing? boolean If false, a missing customer ID causes the broadcast to error and fail. If true, the broadcast will skip over any people in your audience who don't have IDs, and continue sending to the rest of your audience.
---@field rate_limit? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase0RateLimit Lets people enter the broadcast at a fixed rate instead of all at the same time. For a broadcast with one message, this is the send rate. Later messages in a longer workflow follow your workflow and can go out faster. We determine your audience once, on the first run, and the trigger counts toward your queue limit until everyone enters, the send expires, or you cancel it. See [Limit the send rate](/messaging/send/broadcasts/api-triggered-broadcasts/#rate-limit).
---@field scheduled_at? number Unix timestamp (in seconds) when the broadcast will send. Omit it or set it to `0` to send right away. We reject a timestamp more than 5 minutes in the past. Scheduling also changes when we work out your audience: `ids`, `emails`, `per_user_data`, and `data_file_url` set a fixed audience when you make this request, while a `recipients` filter runs when the send fires.

---Contains information you want to use to populate your broadcast.
---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase0DataMap { [string]: any }

---Lets people enter the broadcast at a fixed rate instead of all at the same time. For a broadcast with one message, this is the send rate. Later messages in a longer workflow follow your workflow and can go out faster. We determine your audience once, on the first run, and the trigger counts toward your queue limit until everyone enters, the send expires, or you cancel it. See [Limit the send rate](/messaging/send/broadcasts/api-triggered-broadcasts/#rate-limit).
---@class customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase0RateLimit
---@field period customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase0RateLimitPeriod|string The length of each period.
---@field rate number The maximum number of people that enter the broadcast in each `period`.
---@field spread? boolean When `true`, we let people in at an even pace across the period, once a minute or less often. When `false`, we let the full `rate` in at the start of each period.

---The length of each period.
---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase0RateLimitPeriod "minute"|"hour"|"day"

---Send your broadcast to a group of people defined by a set of conditions.
---@class customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1
---@field recipients customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1Recipients Use `and`, `or`, and `not` to combine segment and attribute conditions. The top-level object accepts one property; nest groups for complex filters.
---@field data? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1DataMap Contains information you want to use to populate your broadcast.
---@field email_add_duplicates? boolean an email address associated with more than one profile id is an error.
---@field email_ignore_missing? boolean If false, a missing email causes the broadcast to error and fail. If true, the broadcast will skip over any people in your audience who don't have emails, and continue sending to the rest of your audience.
---@field expires_after? number Number of seconds after the send starts that the broadcast should stop sending. Omit or set to `0` if you don't want the broadcast to expire. A rate-limited send always expires: if you set `rate_limit` and omit this field or set it to `0`, we set it to 30 days. If the broadcast expires before it finishes sending, Customer.io discards the messages that haven't gone out yet instead of delivering them late. The window runs from `scheduled_at` when you schedule the send, and from the time we receive this request when you don't.
---@field filter? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1Filter Use `and`, `or`, and `not` to combine segment, attribute, and device attribute conditions. The top-level object accepts one property; nest groups for complex filters.
---@field id_ignore_missing? boolean If false, a missing customer ID causes the broadcast to error and fail. If true, the broadcast will skip over any people in your audience who don't have IDs, and continue sending to the rest of your audience.
---@field rate_limit? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1RateLimit Lets people enter the broadcast at a fixed rate instead of all at the same time. For a broadcast with one message, this is the send rate. Later messages in a longer workflow follow your workflow and can go out faster. We determine your audience once, on the first run, and the trigger counts toward your queue limit until everyone enters, the send expires, or you cancel it. See [Limit the send rate](/messaging/send/broadcasts/api-triggered-broadcasts/#rate-limit).
---@field scheduled_at? number Unix timestamp (in seconds) when the broadcast will send. Omit it or set it to `0` to send right away. We reject a timestamp more than 5 minutes in the past. Scheduling also changes when we work out your audience: `ids`, `emails`, `per_user_data`, and `data_file_url` set a fixed audience when you make this request, while a `recipients` filter runs when the send fires.

---Contains information you want to use to populate your broadcast.
---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1DataMap { [string]: any }

---Use `and`, `or`, and `not` to combine segment, attribute, and device attribute conditions. The top-level object accepts one property; nest groups for complex filters.
---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1Filter customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase1|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase2|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase3|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase4|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase5

---@class customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0
---@field ["and"]? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndList Returns results matching *all* conditions.

---@class customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItem
---@field attribute? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemAttribute Filter your audience by attribute.
---@field device_attribute? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemDeviceAttribute Filter your audience by the devices people have. We match a person if any of their devices meets the condition. To match people who have any device at all, set `field` to `id` and `operator` to `exists`.
---@field ["not"]? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemNot Returns people who don't match the condition inside it. `not` takes a single object, not an array. That object can be one condition, or an `and` or `or` group when you want to exclude people who match a combination of conditions.
---@field ["or"]? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemOrList Returns results matching *any* conditions.
---@field segment? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemSegment Provide the `id` of a segment containing people you want to search for.

---Filter your audience by attribute.
---@class customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemAttribute
---@field field string The name of the attribute you want to filter against.
---@field operator customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemAttributeOperator|string Determine how to evaluate criteria against the field—`exists` returns results if a person in the audience has the attribute; `eq` returns results if the audience has the attribute and the attribute has the `value` you specify.
---@field inverse? boolean Set to `true` to match people who *don't* meet the condition.
---@field value? string The value you want to match for this attribute. You must include a value if you use the `eq` operator.

---Determine how to evaluate criteria against the field—`exists` returns results if a person in the audience has the attribute; `eq` returns results if the audience has the attribute and the attribute has the `value` you specify.
---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemAttributeOperator "eq"|"exists"

---Filter your audience by the devices people have. We match a person if any of their devices meets the condition. To match people who have any device at all, set `field` to `id` and `operator` to `exists`.
---@class customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemDeviceAttribute
---@field field string The name of the device attribute you want to filter against. Use `id` to match people who have a device.
---@field operator customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemDeviceAttributeOperator|string Determine how to evaluate criteria against the field—`exists` returns results if a person has a device with the attribute; `eq` returns results if a person has a device with the attribute and the attribute has the `value` you specify.
---@field inverse? boolean Set to `true` to match people who *don't* have a device meeting the condition.
---@field value? string The value you want to match for this device attribute. You must include a value if you use the `eq` operator.

---Determine how to evaluate criteria against the field—`exists` returns results if a person has a device with the attribute; `eq` returns results if a person has a device with the attribute and the attribute has the `value` you specify.
---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemDeviceAttributeOperator "eq"|"exists"

---Returns people who don't match the condition inside it. `not` takes a single object, not an array. That object can be one condition, or an `and` or `or` group when you want to exclude people who match a combination of conditions.
---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemNot customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemNotCase0|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemNotCase1|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemNotCase2|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemNotCase3|customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase1FilterCase0AndItemNotCase4

