---An array of IDs you want to send a broadcast to. **NOTE**: If your workspace identifies people by `email`, don't use this option. Identify your audience by `emails` instead.
---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase3IdsList string[]

---Lets people enter the broadcast at a fixed rate instead of all at the same time. For a broadcast with one message, this is the send rate. Later messages in a longer workflow follow your workflow and can go out faster. We determine your audience once, on the first run, and the trigger counts toward your queue limit until everyone enters, the send expires, or you cancel it. See [Limit the send rate](/messaging/send/broadcasts/api-triggered-broadcasts/#rate-limit).
---@class customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase3RateLimit
---@field period customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase3RateLimitPeriod|string The length of each period.
---@field rate number The maximum number of people that enter the broadcast in each `period`.
---@field spread? boolean When `true`, we let people in at an even pace across the period, once a minute or less often. When `false`, we let the full `rate` in at the start of each period.

---The length of each period.
---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase3RateLimitPeriod "minute"|"hour"|"day"

---An array of JSON objects containing `id` or `email` keys and a `data` key. Each object represents a person you want to send the broadcast to and data you want to personalize their message with using liquid.
---@class customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase4
---@field per_user_data customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase4PerUserDataList The people you want to send a broadcast to, with custom data to personalize each message. Each person must already exist in your workspace—a broadcast trigger can't create people.
---@field data? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase4DataMap Contains information you want to use to populate your broadcast.
---@field email_add_duplicates? boolean an email address associated with more than one profile id is an error.
---@field email_ignore_missing? boolean If false, a missing email causes the broadcast to error and fail. If true, the broadcast will skip over any people in your audience who don't have emails, and continue sending to the rest of your audience.
---@field expires_after? number Number of seconds after the send starts that the broadcast should stop sending. Omit or set to `0` if you don't want the broadcast to expire. A rate-limited send always expires: if you set `rate_limit` and omit this field or set it to `0`, we set it to 30 days. If the broadcast expires before it finishes sending, Customer.io discards the messages that haven't gone out yet instead of delivering them late. The window runs from `scheduled_at` when you schedule the send, and from the time we receive this request when you don't.
---@field filter? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase4Filter Use `and`, `or`, and `not` to combine segment, attribute, and device attribute conditions. The top-level object accepts one property; nest groups for complex filters.
---@field id_ignore_missing? boolean If false, a missing customer ID causes the broadcast to error and fail. If true, the broadcast will skip over any people in your audience who don't have IDs, and continue sending to the rest of your audience.
---@field rate_limit? customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase4RateLimit Lets people enter the broadcast at a fixed rate instead of all at the same time. For a broadcast with one message, this is the send rate. Later messages in a longer workflow follow your workflow and can go out faster. We determine your audience once, on the first run, and the trigger counts toward your queue limit until everyone enters, the send expires, or you cancel it. See [Limit the send rate](/messaging/send/broadcasts/api-triggered-broadcasts/#rate-limit).
---@field scheduled_at? number Unix timestamp (in seconds) when the broadcast will send. Omit it or set it to `0` to send right away. We reject a timestamp more than 5 minutes in the past. Scheduling also changes when we work out your audience: `ids`, `emails`, `per_user_data`, and `data_file_url` set a fixed audience when you make this request, while a `recipients` filter runs when the send fires.

---Contains information you want to use to populate your broadcast.
---@alias customerio.TriggerBroadcastRequestBodyCase4DataMap { [string]: any }

