function Client:check_collection_source(input) end

---Create a file asset
---
---Creates a new file asset.
---
---Accepted file types: `image/bmp`, `image/jpeg`, `image/jpg`, `image/png`, `image/gif`, `application/pdf`. Maximum file size: 2 MB. Maximum image dimensions: 4096px.
---
---`POST /v1/assets/files`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input customerio.CreateAssetRequest
---@return customerio.CreateAssetResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_asset(input) end

---Create a folder
---
---Creates a new folder for organizing file assets. Folder names must be unique within the same parent folder.
---
---`POST /v1/assets/folders`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input customerio.CreateAssetFolderRequest
---@return customerio.CreateAssetFolderResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_asset_folder(input) end

---Connect a collection source
---
---Connect a bucket in Amazon S3, Google Cloud Storage, or Azure Blob Storage so that you can load files from it into your collections. After you connect a source, send its `id` and a file `path` to [write to a collection](/integrations/api/app/tag/collections/submitCollectionWrite/), or [sync a collection](/integrations/api/app/tag/collections/putCollectionSync/) to load new files from a folder automatically.
---
---Your credentials need permission to list and read the bucket:
---
---- **S3:** `s3:ListBucket` and `s3:GetObject`.
---- **Google Cloud Storage:** the Storage Object Viewer role.
---- **Azure:** a container SAS URL that grants read and list (`sp=rl`).
---
---Before Customer.io saves the source, it lists the bucket under your `prefix` and reads the first file it finds. If the bucket has no files under the prefix yet, Customer.io can only check that your credentials list the bucket. Customer.io encrypts your credentials and never returns them.
---
---`POST /v1/collections/sources`
---Errors: BadRequest, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input? customerio.CreateCollectionSourceRequest
---@return customerio.CreateCollectionSourceResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_collection_source(input) end

---Create a manual segment
---
---Create a manual segment with a name and a description. This request creates an empty segment. You can't create a data-driven or snapshot segment with this endpoint.
---
---`POST /v1/segments`
---Errors: BadRequest.
---@param input customerio.CreateManSegmentRequest
---@return customerio.CreateManSegmentResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_man_segment(input) end

---Create and send a one-time send
---
---Create a one-time send (referred to as a "newsletter" in our APIs) and optionally schedule it or send it immediately.
---
---Set the audience with either `recipients` (a filter over segments and profile attributes) or `recipient_file_url` (a CSV of recipients). One of the two is required, and a request carrying both is rejected.
---
---To send it immediately, set `send_now` to `true`. To schedule for later, set `scheduled_at` to a Unix timestamp in the future. If you don't set either, it's created as a draft.
---
---If you set `send_now` or `scheduled_at` and a recipient segment is still building, Customer.io accepts the request and [holds the send](/messaging/send/broadcasts/one-time-sends/#queued-sends) until the segment finishes. The [send](/integrations/api/app/tag/send-messages/sendNewsletter/) and [schedule](/integrations/api/app/tag/send-messages/scheduleNewsletter/) endpoints describe what the one-time send reports while Customer.io holds it.
---
---A `recipient_file_url` audience resolves in the background, so you can't send or schedule in the same request. Poll [Get a one-time send](/integrations/api/app/tag/newsletters/getNewsletters/) until `recipient_file_status` is `done`, then call [send](/integrations/api/app/tag/send-messages/sendNewsletter/) or [schedule](/integrations/api/app/tag/send-messages/scheduleNewsletter/).
---
---There's no endpoint that updates a one-time send, so `name`, the audience, and `deduped` are fixed once you create it. To change them on a draft, delete it and create a new one. You can still edit content through the [variant endpoints](/integrations/api/app/tag/newsletter-variants/listNewsletterVariants/) until it sends.
---
---If you [enabled a subscription center](/journeys/channels/subscriptions/center/#enable-sub-center) in your workspace, `subscription_topic_id` is required. Use the [subscription center endpoint](/integrations/api/app/tag/subscription-center/getTopics/) to find IDs.
---
---Use standard HTML/CSS for the `body` of an email; this endpoint can't pull in global style variables or render our Design Studio's component syntax. You can create Design Studio emails through [other endpoints](/integrations/api/design-studio/). All requests must be less than 1 MB.
---
---`POST /v1/newsletters`
---Errors: BadRequest, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input customerio.CreateNewsletterRequest
---@return customerio.CreateNewsletterResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_newsletter(input) end

---Add a translation to a one-time send
---
---Add a language variant to a one-time send (referred to as a "newsletter" in our APIs).
---
---If you omit optional fields, the values from the default template are copied over untranslated. Make sure you translate all aspects of your default template.
---
---You can't add language variants to a one-time send that has already been sent. You can't manage emails created with the drag-and-drop editor or Design Studio via this endpoint—use [Create an email translation](/integrations/api/design-studio/tag/emails/createEmailTranslation/) for Design Studio emails.
---
---If it has A/B tests, use [Add a translation to a one-time send test group](/integrations/api/app/tag/newsletter-variants/createNewsletterTestLanguageVariant/) instead.
---
---`POST /v1/newsletters/{newsletter_id}/language`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input customerio.CreateNewsletterLanguageVariantRequest
---@return customerio.CreateNewsletterLanguageVariantResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_newsletter_language_variant(input) end

---Create an A/B test group for a one-time send
---
---Create a new A/B test group for a one-time send (referred to as a "newsletter" in our APIs). This duplicates the existing one-time send's content into a new test group, allowing you to test different versions of your message.
---
---This endpoint does not require a request body. The new test group is created as a copy of the existing content.
---
---You cannot add test groups to a one-time send that has already been sent.
---
---`POST /v1/newsletters/{newsletter_id}/test_groups`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input customerio.CreateNewsletterTestGroupRequest
---@return customerio.CreateNewsletterTestGroupResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_newsletter_test_group(input) end

---Add a translation to a one-time send test group
---
---Add a language variant to a specific A/B test group in a one-time send (referred to as a "newsletter" in our APIs). The new variant is a copy of the default template in the test group with the content you provide. The payload the endpoint accepts depends on the parent one-time send's channel type: if it's an email, the payload will be an email variant; if it's an SMS, the payload will be an SMS variant.
---
---You cannot add language variants to a one-time send that has already been sent, or to one-time sends created with the drag-and-drop editor or Design Studio.
---
---`POST /v1/newsletters/{newsletter_id}/test_group/{test_group_id}/language`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input customerio.CreateNewsletterTestLanguageVariantRequest
---@return customerio.CreateNewsletterTestLanguageVariantResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_newsletter_test_language_variant(input) end

